  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 109 AM CDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nAs of 1 AM CDT, temperatures across the region are in the mid 50s to \nlow 60s with light winds generally out of the east to southeast. Low \npressure develops off the Rockies today bringing precipitation \nchances all day and a chance for severe weather this evening, 40-\n70%. There is a Marginal risk (level 1 out of 5) for severe weather \nwith these storms. Main hazards are 1 inch hail and 60-70 mph wind \ngusts. PWATs over the area are in the 1.25 to 1.5 inch range which \ncould also result in brief heavy rainfall. CAMs are in pretty much 2 \ncamps as to when and where the majority of the storms will take \nplace. The first develops in south central SD at around 7 PM CDT and \nintensifies as it moves east across the southern portion of the CWA. \nThe second moves into the area out of ND closer to midnight CDT, \nmoves east and intensifies into northeast SD. Both camps have storms \nout of the area by sunrise Saturday morning. There is also a Slight \nrisk (level 2 out of 5) for portions of north central SD and a \nMarginal risk for areas west of the Prairie Coteau/Sisseton Hills \nSaturday as the low moves off the Rockies. Following this, low level \nprecipitation chances remain in place most days as a series of low \npressure systems move across southern Canada.\n\nTemperatures through the period remain around to slightly above \naverage. Some light elevated smoke will move into the area today, \nresulting in hazy skies. Winds across south central SD will gust 25-\n30 mph and these look to be the highest winds through the 7-day. We \ncould begin to see some elevated fire danger next work week if we \ndon't get much rain out of these storms.",
